blurb = "Depicts the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mita_Hachiman_Shrine]Mita Hachiman Shrine[/url] at Tamachi in the Shiba district (within present-day Tōkyō) atop a wooded hill. Several visitors pause in the courtyard to view the full moon overhead.

The shrine was allegedly founded in 1365, and a shrine rebuilt in 1957 still stands on the same site. A guardian dog statue on the grounds was dedicated in 1696.

From the series Eight Views of Shiba in the Eastern Capital."
